  { "ref": "Ex 7.8 Q13", "book_key": "(not on provided AK page)", "our_answer": "\\tfrac{1}{2}\\log 2", "verdict": "CANT-READ-KEY", "note": "The reprint 2025-26 AK (ak-06) lists Exercise 7.8 answers 1-12 only; our data's Q13-22 correspond to the old Exercise 7.9 numbering and have no key entry on the provided page. Independently re-derived: \\int_2^3 x/(x^2+1)dx=\\tfrac12[\\log(x^2+1)]_2^3=\\tfrac12(\\log10-\\log5)=\\tfrac12\\log2 — OUR ANSWER CORRECT. Flagged for manual key check." },
  { "ref": "Ex 7.8 Q14", "book_key": "(not on provided AK page)", "our_answer": "\\tfrac{1}{5}\\log 6+\\tfrac{3}{\\sqrt5}\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt5", "verdict": "CANT-READ-KEY", "note": "No key on provided page (reprint Ex 7.8 lists 1-12 only). Re-derived: \\int_0^1(2x+3)/(5x^2+1)dx=\\tfrac15\\log(5x^2+1)|_0^1+\\tfrac{3}{\\sqrt5}\\tan^{-1}(\\sqrt5 x)|_0^1=\\tfrac15\\log6+\\tfrac{3}{\\sqrt5}\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt5 — OUR ANSWER CORRECT." },
  { "ref": "Ex 7.8 Q15", "book_key": "(not on provided AK page)", "our_answer": "\\tfrac{1}{2}(e-1)", "verdict": "CANT-READ-KEY", "note": "No key on provided page. Re-derived: t=x^2, \\int_0^1 x e^{x^2}dx=\\tfrac12\\int_0^1 e^t dt=\\tfrac12(e-1) — OUR ANSWER CORRECT." },
  { "ref": "Ex 7.8 Q16", "book_key": "(not on provided AK page)", "our_answer": "5+\\tfrac{5}{2}\\log\\tfrac{3}{2}-\\tfrac{45}{2}\\log\\tfrac{5}{4}", "verdict": "CANT-READ-KEY", "note": "No key on provided page. Re-derived: 5x^2/(x^2+4x+3)=5-(20x+15)/((x+1)(x+3))=5+5/(2(x+1))-45/(2(x+3)); antideriv 5x+\\tfrac52\\log(x+1)-\\tfrac{45}{2}\\log(x+3), eval 1..2 = 5+\\tfrac52\\log\\tfrac32-\\tfrac{45}{2}\\log\\tfrac54 — OUR ANSWER CORRECT." },
  { "ref": "Ex 7.8 Q17", "book_key": "(not on provided AK page)", "our_answer": "2+\\tfrac{\\pi^4}{1024}+\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}", "verdict": "CANT-READ-KEY", "note": "No key on provided page. Re-derived: [2\\tan x+x^4/4+2x]_0^{\\pi/4}=2+(\\pi/4)^4/4+\\pi/2=2+\\pi^4/1024+\\pi/2 — OUR ANSWER CORRECT." },
  { "ref": "Ex 7.8 Q18", "book_key": "(not on provided AK page)", "our_answer": "0", "verdict": "CANT-READ-KEY", "note": "No key on provided page. Re-derived: \\sin^2(x/2)-\\cos^2(x/2)=-\\cos x, \\int_0^\\pi -\\cos x\\,dx=-[\\sin x]_0^\\pi=0 — OUR ANSWER CORRECT." },
  { "ref": "Ex 7.8 Q19", "book_key": "(not on provided AK page)", "our_answer": "3\\log 2+\\tfrac{3\\pi}{8}", "verdict": "CANT-READ-KEY", "note": "No key on provided page. Re-derived: [3\\log(x^2+4)+\\tfrac32\\tan^{-1}(x/2)]_0^2=3(\\log8-\\log4)+\\tfrac32\\cdot\\tfrac\\pi4=3\\log2+\\tfrac{3\\pi}{8} — OUR ANSWER CORRECT." },
  { "ref": "Ex 7.8 Q20", "book_key": "(not on provided AK page)", "our_answer": "1+\\tfrac{4-2\\sqrt2}{\\pi}", "verdict": "CANT-READ-KEY", "note": "No key on provided page. Re-derived: \\int_0^1 xe^x dx=[(x-1)e^x]_0^1=1; \\int_0^1\\sin(\\pi x/4)dx=\\tfrac4\\pi(1-\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2})=(4-2\\sqrt2)/\\pi; sum=1+(4-2\\sqrt2)/\\pi — OUR ANSWER CORRECT." },
  { "ref": "Ex 7.8 Q21", "book_key": "(not on provided AK page)", "our_answer": "D", "verdict": "CANT-READ-KEY", "note": "MCQ; no key on provided page. Re-derived: \\int_1^{\\sqrt3}dx/(1+x^2)=\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt3-\\tan^{-1}1=\\pi/3-\\pi/4=\\pi/12; our letter D — consistent with old NCERT key (D=\\pi/12). Flagged for manual key check." },
  { "ref": "Ex 7.8 Q22", "book_key": "(not on provided AK page)", "our_answer": "C", "verdict": "CANT-READ-KEY", "note": "MCQ; no key on provided page. Re-derived: \\int_0^{2/3}dx/(4+9x^2)=\\tfrac16\\tan^{-1}(3x/2)|_0^{2/3}=\\tfrac16\\tan^{-1}1=\\pi/24; our letter C — consistent with old NCERT key (C=\\pi/24). Flagged for manual key check." }
